From d5aad5cab5db75a2128c301b449539dde99dd5b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rou <shamay1030@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 15:01:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/27] NOC: semantic sub-context KV reuse and
 position-independent KV linking

Adds the LegoLink / PICRuntime research stack on top of upstream SGLang
cd012ad. Previously this existed only as uncommitted working-tree state.

New modules (python/sglang/srt/):
- pic_runtime.py: PICRuntime.run_link (lookup -> KV relocation -> RoPE
  global-position remap -> request-private write-back -> sparse boundary
  repair -> native decode handoff), PICRequestTokenRegistry._prepare_link
  which rebuilds the authoritative LinkPlan from RadixCache block tokens,
  plus CUDA-Event / host-timing / JSONL trace instrumentation.
- legolink_triton.py: optional Triton kernel fusing KV gather, RoPE delta
  rotation and scatter, with a boundary-repair-aware stale-row skip and a
  guarded per-architecture launch config.
- flashinfer_sparse_repair.py: FlashInfer attention operator for sparse
  boundary repair (paged-prefill FA2 rows and block-sparse rows), sparse
  metadata construction, wrapper/plan caches and fail-closed selection.
- sparse_repair_compute.py: repair-row batch planning, execution units and
  row-wise FFN / output-projection slicing that preserves per-row numerics.

Modified upstream files:
- mem_cache/radix_cache.py: LegoLink semantic block registry living inside
  RadixCache (register/lookup/acquire/pin/evict, compatibility keys,
  generation invalidation, execution accounting). RadixCache remains the KV
  storage, ownership and cache-management layer.
- managers/scheduler.py, scheduler_components/batch_result_processor.py:
  link-request admission, source-block reservation, batch isolation, and
  pinning of finished Compile blocks.
- model_executor/model_runner.py, forward_batch_info.py: PIC dispatch with
  fail-closed / fallback modes and phase instrumentation.
- entrypoints/openai/*: sub_context and pic_link request fields with
  physical-token count and SHA-256 validation.
- layers/radix_attention.py, models/qwen2.py: sparse-repair attention
  handoff and row-wise FFN / output projection.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
